<title>UK: Camelot extends BBC contract by 12 months.</title>
<headline>Camelot extends BBC contract by 12 months.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British lottery operator Camelot Group Plc said on Thursday it would extend the BBC's contract to broadcast the lottery for 12 months from November.</p>
<p>The contract was due for renewal in November.</p>
<p>Camelot said that it would explore options for broadcasting arrangements beyond November 1998 with the BBC and ITV companies over the next year.</p>
<p>Camelot is a consortium of Racal Electronics Plc, De La Rue Plc, GTECH, Cadbury Schweppes Plc and Fujitsu Ltd's ICL.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
